# Copy to `secrets.env` at the REPO ROOT and fill in. Every module resolves this one file from
# __file__, so it loads no matter which directory you run from.
#
#   cp secrets.env.example secrets.env
#
# `secrets.env` is gitignored. This example file is not — keep real keys/paths out of it.
#
# Renamed from api.env 2026-07-28, then config.env -> secrets.env 2026-08-24. It holds API keys,
# tokens, and machine-specific paths. "config.env" confused people into reaching for runconfig.toml
# and understated that this file carries credentials; "secrets.env" makes the contents obvious.

# --- Agent runtime: OpenAI API compatible endpoint -------------------------------
# Shared OpenAI-compatible LLM transport. vllm is the default and preserves the legacy settings.
LLM_PROVIDER=vllm
# Any server speaking the OpenAI Chat Completions API works for the vllm profile.
# Retired OpenRouter for agent calls (2026-07-19 user directive) when its credits ran out.
# OPENAI_API_URL owns scheme, host, and port; clients append /v1.
# The endpoint 401s without a bearer key (measured 2026-07-19).
OPENAI_API_URL=http://your-endpoint-host:8000
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Vertex alternative (uses Application Default Credentials; no static access token or gcloud call).
# LLM_PROVIDER=vertex
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=your-project-id
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=global
# OPENAI_MODEL=google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# --- Agent runtime: model selection ----------------------------------------------
# The model id the endpoint above is asked for. This is the ONE place to change it: every
# agent-runtime reasoner (orchestrator, actor, associative memory, perception, item resolver,
# planners, probes) reads it via agent_core.models. Unset falls back to Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B.
# OPENAI_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B

# The offline annotator's model when run with `--backend endpoint`.
# Defaults to OPENAI_MODEL when unset. The default `claude-cli` annotator backend is NOT affected —
# it carries its own --model (sonnet, the frozen quality baseline; see agent/CLAUDE.md).
# OPENAI_ANNOTATOR_MODEL=

# --- Unity sim: filesystem -------------------------------------------------------
# The Unity project is a SEPARATE repo (see agent/CLAUDE.md) - there is no path to it that
# works across machines, so it is not guessed or hardcoded. agent/sim/sim_paths.py reads these.
#
# Root of the Unity sim repo — the folder that contains Assets/Resources/Data/*.json (Categories.json,
# PriceData.json). Used by the completion guard's catalog grounding (orchestrator/subtask_completion.py)
# and the offline scoring/reconciliation scripts (mapping/scoring/*.py). Grounding degrades gracefully
# to plain substring matching when unset; the scoring scripts require it and fail loudly without it.
# SARI_SANDBOX_DIR=/path/to/SariSandboxV2

# The Unity save file the sim writes at runtime (shelf placements ground truth for score_index.py's
# per-slot scoring). Typically under Unity's persistentDataPath, e.g. on Windows:
#   C:\Users\<you>\AppData\LocalLow\Sari Sandbox\Sari Sandbox V2\Store 2 v2.json
# SARI_STORE_SAVE_JSON=/path/to/Store 2 v2.json

# --- Unity sim: network ------------------------------------------------------------
# The sim's WebSocket command server. agent/sim/env.py reads this (resolved per call, so
# the --ws-uri option in run_agent.py can override it at runtime); md_tools.py and the mapping
# scripts still carry their own hardcoded defaults. Distributed Sari Bench sets it per attempt to
# the sandbox it leased, which is how several agents run against different sims at once.
# SARI_WS_URI=ws://localhost:8080/commands

# --- Central OCR service ----------------------------------------------------------
# Every agent sends in-memory PNG receipt crops to one runner-local PaddleOCR daemon. Start it with
# `uv run poe ocr-server`; on the configured Windows/WSL AMD host that command launches the native
# DirectML daemon automatically. Flags named --ocr-url take precedence over this variable; the
# final default is http://127.0.0.1:9100. Agents never construct a local Paddle model or fall back.
# SARI_OCR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9100
# `python -m sari_bench ocr-server` uses DirectML automatically when run in a Windows environment
# that provides it. Override with paddle, onnx-cpu, or directml when launching the server directly.
# SARI_OCR_BACKEND=auto

# --- Third-party -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Moondream cloud API — the agent runtime's only non-self-hosted dependency.
# Used by md_tools.py and perception.py.
MDREAM_API_KEY=

# Gemini — legacy root stack (functions.py, comprehension.py).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — LEGACY. Credits exhausted (402); agent calls moved to the OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# Still read by agent.py's OpenRouterConfig default and subagent_run.py.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Replicate — no reader found anywhere in the codebase. Present in the original
# api.env; safe to drop unless something outside this repo uses it.
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# --- sari_bench watch: Discord notifications --------------------------------------
# The dashboard watcher (sari_bench/watch, started with --discord) posts battery/attempt updates
# to this webhook. See sari_bench/watch/notify.py. Collapse-alert behavior is configured
# separately, in runconfig.toml's [discord] section.
# SARI_BENCH_DISCORD_WEBHOOK=

# --- Legacy root stack -----------------------------------------------------------
# The LitServe inference server that run.py posts to. Hardcoded at run.py:10 today.
# SARI_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8005/predict

# Legacy fallback for OPENAI_API_URL/OPENAI_API_KEY when neither is set above: agent_core.llm and
# annotate_probe.py read a conda-meta state file for machines that invoke sari_env_old's
# python.exe directly (skips the activation hooks that normally set these vars). Only needed if
# you rely on that setup; the hardcoded default is a specific Windows conda install and will not
# exist on most machines, which is fine — it's a last-resort fallback, not a requirement.
# SARI_CONDA_STATE=C:/Sari/sari_env_old/conda-meta/state
